        answer: "With engineered bent frames — each bent is a rigid portal of columns and rafters designed to carry the full snow load across the span without interior supports. The engineer sizes the members for bending and deflection under the unbalanced snow case and designs the rigid joints to transfer the frame moments. Forty to sixty feet is routine for heavy timber or steel bents; the engineering is in the joints, not just the member sizes.",
