        heading: "Terraced Grading, Walls, and Snow Management",
        body: "The engineer works the site in terraces: each parking terrace held to drivable grades, retaining walls engineered with the geotechnical report's soils and drained against spring hydrostatic pressure, and accessible routes threaded at compliant slopes from the accessible stalls to every tenant entry. Snow storage is drawn on the grading plan as deliberately as the parking stalls — sized for the design winter, kept clear of accessible routes and fire access, and graded so meltwater reaches treatment instead of refreezing across the walkways.\n\nWalkway snowmelt is zoned to the pedestrian reality: entries, stairs, and the main promenade melt; secondary areas are plowed. The engineer sizes the snowmelt for the design storm and details the control sequence so the system anticipates the storm rather than chasing it, since a walkway that melts halfway and refreezes is more dangerous than one left snow-covered.",
