        heading: "Ski Village Retail Plaza Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the site plan is submitted:\n\n• Terraced grading with retaining walls designed from the geotechnical report and drained against hydrostatic pressure\n• Accessible parking and routes held to compliant grades on the slope; terrace edges with pedestrian protection\n• Snow-storage areas sized for the design winter, placed to drain meltwater to treatment, clear of access and fire lanes\n• Walkway and entry snowmelt zoned to critical paths and sized for the design storm\n• Tenant shells with capped grease-waste rough-ins, adequate electrical capacity, and adaptable HVAC distribution\n• Roof structure per ASCE 7 snow with drift checked at parapets, anchor-to-shop steps, and walkway canopies; sliding snow detailed away from pedestrians\n• Stormwater treated for winter sand, salt, and petroleum; discharge capacity verified with the town or county\n• Fire access with apparatus reach and setup areas threaded through the terraces; fire-district review early\n• Alpine design review coordinated from schematic design; town vs county permit path confirmed",
